<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kublai Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1215">1215</a>–<a href="/years/1294">1294</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kublai Khan was a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> who became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-khan">Great Khan</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. He completed the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> in 1279 and ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khanbaliq">Khanbaliq</a>. His disputed succession contributed to the fragmentation of the Mongol Empire, and his expeditions overseas, including against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, influenced the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kublai-khan.jpg" alt="Kublai Khan" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Araniko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:YuanEmperorAlbumKhubilaiPortrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
